  "summary": "Early in my career, I saw how often companies built the wrong things. Not out of bad intentions, but because the voice of the user went unheard.\n    \nThat’s why before building Condens, a user research platform for storing, analyzing and sharing data, we spoke to hundreds of user researchers to make sure we truly understood their reality. And their input is what has shaped at lot we’ve built at Condens. \n    \nToday, Condens is a sustainable business serving organizations worldwide by empowering them to de-risk business decisions and bringing them closer to the users they create for. And we’re really just getting started.\n    \nFor me, Condens is proof that when you put users first, everyone wins.",
